{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight","id":1044117,"title":"Understanding Focused Mage Sight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-05T11:58:35-08:00","id":1044117,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Understanding Focused Mage Sight","content":"Hey Everyone,<br /> <br /> So, I have decided I really want to get a full grasp of Focused Mage Sight and what players are capable of doing when they are utilizing it to analyze spells/supernatural phenomena/mundane things.<br /> <br /> I am going to throw out some scenarios and lay out my understanding/interpretation of what I expect mechanical/plot information is derived from scrutinizing and revelation.<br /> <br /> First Scenario:<br /> An Acanthus Mage happens upon an unconscious man in a back alley that seems to have no physical injuries and has no pulse. He suspects this person may have been poisoned or perhaps overdosed on something, but either way he decides to rule out any magical cause for this man's current state and uses Focused Mage Sight to determine what he can see.<br /> <br /> Now, the man is actually under the effect of the Suppress Life spell used by another Mage looking to gain information inside the man's house and has placed him in the street alley to hide him for the time being. The opacity is 2 since it is a Death Ruling Spell and it was an Improvised Spell.<br /> <br /> The Acanthus rolls and gets a couple of successes with his Scrutiny and decides to use the Revelation mechanic to see what information he was able to determine from the analysis of the man lying in the street alley.<br /> <br /> Since he lowered the Opacity to 1 he does not get any deep information, but he does get some Surface Information which details the following:<br /> - Awakened Magic was indeed used on this man<br /> - He determines it is from the Death Arcana and gets the smell of Embalming fluid (the Signature Nimbus of the caster)<br /> - He determines that this effect has been in place for about 30 minutes<br /> <br /> The Acanthus Mage decides that this is sufficient and is familiar with the Signature Nimbus of the caster recognizing it with a fellow order member and decides to send his pal a message letting him know about leaving stuff in street alleys to remind his friend to not forgot the guy.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Acanthus Mage would not know it is the Death Arcana, but maybe Focused Mage Sight can divine a lot of information regardless of what Paths are used.<br /> <br /> Second Scenario:<br /> A Mastigos Mage runs across a very odd woman in a bar that he feels entranced to approach, but he is actually very shy despite having the ability to instantly perceive how people feel about him. However, she feels different and his PMS is driving him nuts every time he glances at her so he decides maybe to focus a little harder on what is so special about this woman at the bar.<br /> <br /> So, the woman is actually a host for Abyssal Spiders, as some might have guessed, and I have rated this Mystery at an opacity 3 since it is like Psychic Domination but since it is not Supernal it is actually multiplied by 1.5 as indicated in the book.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos Mage rolls and gets a couple of successes with his Scrutiny and decides to use the Revelation mechanic to see what information he was able to determine from the analysis of the woman at the bar.<br /> <br /> He was able to lower the Opacity to 2, so he does not get any deep information, but he does get some Surface Information which details the following:<br /> -This mystery is not a result of Awakened Magic.<br /> -This effect has been going on for at least a couple of days.<br /> <br /> This seems appropriate and fits well with what I would expect for most any type of general Focused Mage Sight inquiry regardless of the Path belonging to the Mage.<br /> <br /> Third Scenario:<br /> An Obrimos Mage finds a dagger that supposedly belonged to a notorious assassin that has killed many people, but he is skeptical whether the item is actually the real deal so he decides to use his Focused Mage Sight to glean some information regarding the dagger.<br /> <br /> This dagger is in fact the weapon used by the notorious assassin. The Opacity is 0 since there is no magic involved or anything supernatural, it just happens to be a finely crafted dagger used by a famous assassin.<br /> <br /> The Obrimos Mage rolls and gets a couple of successes with his Scrutiny roll and decides to use the Revelation mechanic to see what information he was able to determine from the analysis of the dagger.<br /> <br /> Since the Mystery had no Opacity he gains Surface Information and Deep Information which details the following:<br /> - This Mystery is not related to Awakened Magic<br /> - This Mystery is 3 years old (when it was first crafted)<br /> - This Mystery does not happen to be revolving around anything in the Supernal or the Abyss.<br /> - This blade was finely crafted and seems to have been used quite frequently with much force.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the long post, but let me know if I am understanding the use of Focused Mage Sight correctly!<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:19:19-08:00","id":1044213,"title":"","content":"Scenario 1: Unless the Acanthus is using Death Mage Sight he doesn't learn anything.<br /> <br /> Scenario 2: Seems fine.<br /> <br /> Scenario 3: It's not actually a Mystery in the sense that FMS would work on it so the Obrimos would learn nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T06:05:48-08:00","id":1044460,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Taldor, from what I understand of active mage sight a mage can determine if a supernatural mystery at least partially falls under his path arcana via active mage sight since active mage sight reveals the existence (if not the substance) of supernatural phenomena relating to the arcana of his path. This is one of the reasons for having a cabal. You can save yourself mana and time by having multiple people activate mage sight while observing something supernatural. Mana, since each person won't have to spend mana to activate their secondary arcana sight and time since the wrong kind of focused mage sight reveals nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:02:03-08:00","id":1044480,"title":"","content":"The one exception to the first scenario responses above is the material contained in the preview of Signs of Sorcery (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for-miles-and-miles-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for...the-awakening/</a>). With the rules they included there an Acanthus who succeeded on a Revelation would learn that the Mystery in question pertained to the Death Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3139-rayn-faustus","name":"Rayn Faustus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3139_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:08:01-08:00","id":1044482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayn Faustus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044480#post1044480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one exception to the first scenario responses above is the material contained in the preview of Signs of Sorcery (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for-miles-and-miles-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for...the-awakening/</a>). With the rules they included there an Acanthus who succeeded on a Revelation would learn that the Mystery in question pertained to the Death Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would only learn that the effect doesn't fall under their Path Arcana, they could check with Death if they have it. This doesn't require Revelation, it's just a process of elimination by finding what's getting traction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:19:27-08:00","id":1044487,"title":"","content":"From the document I linked: &quot;<i>If a mage does not have the appropriate Arcana active in her Mage Sight, she may still attempt to Reveal the Mystery. If she succeeds, however, the only Surface Information she receives is which Arcanum's purview the Mystery falls under.&quot;</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3139-rayn-faustus","name":"Rayn Faustus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3139_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T07:47:28-08:00","id":1044503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rayn Faustus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044487#post1044487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the document I linked: &amp;quot;<i>If a mage does not have the appropriate Arcana active in her Mage Sight, she may still attempt to Reveal the Mystery. If she succeeds, however, the only Surface Information she receives is which Arcanum's purview the Mystery falls under.&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Second paragraph under System in Focused Mage Sight section says otherwise. Probably your example trumps mine as Revelation modifies that general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:03:35-08:00","id":1044513,"title":"","content":"Yeah it wouldn't have been possible based on just the core material, but they seem to want to open things up a bit with the rules in Signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3139-rayn-faustus","name":"Rayn Faustus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3139_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:14:11-08:00","id":1044518,"title":"","content":"Not quite got my head around the new Mage sight mechanics myself so this also helped me. All this talk of mysteries is taking a bit of getting used to, i need to keep reminding myself that anything odd/supernatural is basically a mystery so thanks. But just a quickie..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight#post1044117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Everyone,<br /> <br /> Now, the man is actually under the effect of the Suppress Life spell used by another Mage looking to gain information inside the man's house and has placed him in the street alley to hide him for the time being. The opacity is 2 since it is a Death Ruling Spell and it was an Improvised Spell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Suppress life does not actually make people drop down and act dead, (errata document mentions it but it isnt in the post errata pdf though) its a veiling spell, all it does it make somebody appear dead, which if they happen to be walking about really wont matter unless your trying to get into a zombie club or something. I know it doesnt make a difference in the example but<br /> <br /> Also how do you get the opacity of cast spells? Is it just the level of arcana used? You mentioned it was a improvised spell so does ritual casting increase opacity?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:32:32-08:00","id":1044525,"title":"","content":"Something that gets my attention: How would the Mage even know there's something magical going on? Does Mage Sight reveal the presence of magical phenomena regardless of type? Or does it have to be within the purview of the arcana they're looking with?<br /> <br /> It gets trickier with the presence of the Signature Nimbus on the target. Are they and the spell the same Mystery or a different one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:37:38-08:00","id":1044528,"title":"","content":"Periphereal Mage sight alerts you there's something magical going on, no matter your Path or Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T08:38:42-08:00","id":1044530,"title":"","content":"Passive Mage Sight already reveals the presence of all active magical effects regardless of source or type. Active Mage Sight reveals what it is that pings the Passive version if you activate it with the right Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:20:08-08:00","id":1044553,"title":"","content":"Unless it's Veiling, in which case PMS doesn't ping, but AMS of an appropriate arcana would provoke a CoW. Suppress Life being a Veiling effect a Mage wouldn't have a PMS alert to anything magical happening.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> There are guidelines for setting opacity in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:22:07-08:00","id":1044557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044530#post1044530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Passive Mage Sight already reveals the presence of all active magical effects regardless of source or type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Active in front of you - if you meet Thyrsus that is having <i>Honing the Form</i> casted from few days ago on whole week ( meaning he will have still few days worth of it, always turn on ) you will <i>not </i>feel his effect. He would need to cast in the same scene as you are nearby to your Passive Mage Sight to *ping*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:24:08-08:00","id":1044560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044557#post1044557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Active in front of you - if you meet Thyrsus that is having <i>Honing the Form</i> casted from few days ago on whole week ( meaning he will have still few days worth of it, always turn on ) you will <i>not </i>feel his effect. He would need to cast in the same scene as you are nearby to your Passive Mage Sight to *ping*.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's right, source?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:28:48-08:00","id":1044561,"title":"","content":"You'd see his signature nimbus on it, at least with focused sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:17:14-08:00","id":1044591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044213#post1044213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario 3: It's not actually a Mystery in the sense that FMS would work on it so the Obrimos would learn nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a><br /> <br /> This Scenario I am perplexed by because from your understanding no information is gained, but from the Core Rulebook the following text states this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Obrimos sees the same knife in terms of all the energy that was put into it, and knows a faulty blade because it diverges too much from its platonic ideal. </div> </div> </div>Which sight is being used here to gain this information. I assumed this was Focused Mage Sight, but if I was wrong I am curious which Mage Sight is being referred to for this example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 02-06-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:25:28-08:00","id":1044598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044591#post1044591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> This Scenario I am perplexed by because from your understanding no information is gained, but from the Core Rulebook the following text states this:<br /> <br /> <br /> Which sight is being used here to gain this information. I assumed this was Focused Mage Sight, but if I was wrong I am curious which Mage Sight is being referred to for this example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where you're pulling that from so I can't give you an opinion because I lack context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:30:04-08:00","id":1044601,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>,<br /> <br /> That was a quote from the Eyes Wide Open section in the Core Rulebook on pg. 66 the second paragraph on the top left of that page.<br /> <br /> Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:30:35-08:00","id":1044602,"title":"","content":"It's on p66.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:46:09-08:00","id":1044611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044560#post1044560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's right, source?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the case as far as I'm aware as well. The book notes that Peripheral Sight is pinged by supernatural occurrences, but not &quot;passive&quot; entities. A ghost hovering in Twilight is not pinged (without the Death 2 attainment) unless it uses one of its Numina. Likewise, a vampire doesn't ping your senses without using its vampire powers, despite being a walking corpse.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure Dave has elaborated on this too, but I can't really find where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:37:05-08:00","id":1044634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044611#post1044611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the case as far as I'm aware as well. The book notes that Peripheral Sight is pinged by supernatural occurrences, but not &amp;quot;passive&amp;quot; entities. A ghost hovering in Twilight is not pinged (without the Death 2 attainment) unless it uses one of its Numina. Likewise, a vampire doesn't ping your senses without using its vampire powers, despite being a walking corpse.<br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure Dave has elaborated on this too, but I can't really find where.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> is talking about active spells not pinging PMS after they're cast, unlike a ghost just hanging out though, spells (With the pseudo-exception of Veiling) aren't passive they are an active use of a Mage's power regardless of how long ago they've been brought into existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:43:38-08:00","id":1044635,"title":"","content":"Unless I've missed something Veiling as a Practice isn't automatically an exception to the rule. It's just that supernatural means of hiding something won't register on PMS and all Veiling spells naturally deals with hiding stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T11:57:12-08:00","id":1044642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044635#post1044635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I've missed something Veiling as a Practice isn't automatically an exception to the rule. It's just that supernatural means of hiding something won't register on PMS and all Veiling spells naturally deals with hiding stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my saying it's only a pseudo-exception, in that it may look like an exception but it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:06:00-08:00","id":1044647,"title":"","content":"Anyway, having looked it over, I think Scenario 3 is probably also correct. If the Obrimos used Prime MS he's probably also be able to read its resonance which could reveal clues about the forceful use to which the knife had been put. It wouldn't verify the authenticity of the knife in any specific way though. So, you might know you have a knife that's been used for killing, maybe even as specific as assassination, but you wouldn't be able to determine that it was used by Georgovitch and that he lost it during his famous slaying of the king in 1543.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-06-2017, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:17:36-08:00","id":1044763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044634#post1044634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> is talking about active spells not pinging PMS after they're cast, unlike a ghost just hanging out though, spells (With the pseudo-exception of Veiling) aren't passive they are an active use of a Mage's power regardless of how long ago they've been brought into existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seemed to recall a prior discussion on the topic that led to the Word of God being determined as &quot;Mages don't detect spells after they're cast&quot;, but in searching, I seem to have proven my own memory faulty.<br /> <br /> Per the original Mage Sight spoiler:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages sense the presence of continuing effects like magical wards or spiritual possession until the effect ends or they leave the area. </div> </div> </div>So. That's that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:34:52-08:00","id":1045212,"title":"","content":"The rules are inconsistent.<br /> <br /> I think AMS should detect Wards, but PMS should only detect Wards if Space is used, for instance and that's what I'll do at my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T10:59:46-08:00","id":1045224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1045212#post1045212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules are inconsistent.<br /> <br /> I think AMS should detect Wards, but PMS should only detect Wards if Space is used, for instance and that's what I'll do at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have PMS and AMS confused. Also, that being the case I have to assume you're wrong about the rules being inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:33:11-08:00","id":1045244,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't see a question of consistency, only what defines an active or passive effect or occurrence. An active effect appears to be one which someone willed to occur, a passive one merely something that would be regardless. That, to me, appears to be a consistent definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:02:44-08:00","id":1045804,"title":"","content":"So what you guys are interpreting is that any PMS will detect existing Wards that were cast yesterday?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:27:17-08:00","id":1045815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1045804#post1045804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you guys are interpreting is that any PMS will detect existing Wards that were cast yesterday?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any PMS will detect any currently active spell that isn't a Veiling spell. Furthermore, there is no &quot;any&quot; PMS, there is -only- PMS. Only AMS and FMS differentiate by Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:30:06-08:00","id":1045849,"title":"","content":"That is my interpretation as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:13:24-08:00","id":1045869,"title":"","content":"What Mrm said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:04:07-08:00","id":1046014,"title":"","content":"Ok. That's something I interpreted differently. So even though PMS doesn't detect Ghosts will an active continuous Ghost Numina invoked yesterday still ping PMS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:28:19-08:00","id":1046029,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:28:31-08:00","id":1046056,"title":"","content":"Veiling spells aren't an exception to being detected by PMS. Supernal Veil does explictly say so, but it's the only one. If someone has an active Incognito Presence, the mage may not notice them but will know there's an active spell nerby. If he switches to Active Mage Sight and tries to look closely, then he would have a Clash of Wills, and if he loses he would look away never knowing where the spell came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:30:51-08:00","id":1046058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046014#post1046014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. That's something I interpreted differently. So even though PMS doesn't detect Ghosts will an active continuous Ghost Numina invoked yesterday still ping PMS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Although, if a Mage has Death 2 his PMS will expand to ping when a ghost is nearby in Twilight hanging out too. Same for Mind with Goetia and Spirit with spirits provided they aren't using a concealment power though even in that case the Mage is automatically entitled to a CoW. That's automatic and doesn't cost mana. These are special exceptions granted by the 2nd dot utility attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:32:28-08:00","id":1046059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046056#post1046056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veiling spells aren't an exception to being detected by PMS. Supernal Veil does explictly say so, but it's the only one. If someone has an active Incognito Presence, the mage may not notice them but will know there's an active spell nerby. If he switches to Active Mage Sight and tries to look closely, then he would have a Clash of Wills, and if he loses he would look away never knowing where the spell came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the PMS section: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any supernatural attempt at concealment<br /> hides the effect from the mage, without a Clash of Wills or any<br /> other mechanical effect. </div> </div> </div>So, yes, Veiling spells are an exception to being detected by PMS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:36:58-08:00","id":1046061,"title":"","content":"Ok, but a Memory Hole wouldn't, or a spell hiding Sympathies or a person's past or Destiny. It doesn't say Veiling spells, because not all Veiling spells are about concealment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:43:09-08:00","id":1046064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046061#post1046061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but a Memory Hole wouldn't, or a spell hiding Sympathies or a person's past or Destiny. It doesn't say Veiling spells, because not all Veiling spells are about concealment.</div> </div> </div> </div>All veiling spell's are about concealment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T18:40:44-08:00","id":1046108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046061#post1046061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but a Memory Hole wouldn't, or a spell hiding Sympathies or a person's past or Destiny. It doesn't say Veiling spells, because not all Veiling spells are about concealment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snipped from the Practices section for Veiling:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Firstly, they can conceal things under the Arcanum\u2019s purview from detection...Secondly, they can conceal a target from concrete phenomena under the Arcanum\u2019s purview... </div> </div> </div>So you're wrong again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:33:26-08:00","id":1046132,"title":"","content":"Well, for that you didn't need to go to the book, I said &quot;hiding&quot; myself... But that reading to me is rules-lawery. I don't think that's the intended interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T22:34:08-08:00","id":1046184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1044557#post1044557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Active in front of you - if you meet Thyrsus that is having <i>Honing the Form</i> casted from few days ago on whole week ( meaning he will have still few days worth of it, always turn on ) you will <i>not </i>feel his effect. He would need to cast in the same scene as you are nearby to your Passive Mage Sight to *ping*.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWrong. Passive Mage Sight pings anything when anything is supernatural within LOS not specifically veiled while in LOS and possibly the What if you've seen it before and tried active sight and figured out it's under another arcanum's purview. Active gives you What if you have the correct Arcanum up. Focused gives you How and Why after you figure out the What. Just like detectives, journalists of technical support people.<br /> <br /> 1. Where<br /> 2.When<br /> 3.What<br /> 4.Why<br /> 5.How<br /> <br /> \u200bBasic questions and procedures for all of the above fields or any line of investigation or defense actually. It'd ping unless it was a combination spell that allowed it to be veiled for the entire duration. Which isn't the most efficient use of a combination spell in my opinion unless you plan to hit quick and for all the money, no fooling around. Given Mage Armor is reflexive correct and an attainment correct?<br /> <br /> \u200bLook, I work as technical support for televisions so you're always asking probing questions because very few people correctly describe what they actually see. Let alone having the power to specifically sense and KNOW the unseen actually happened within you're line of sight and have a damn good idea what it might be without investigation. With investigation (active mage sight) you have more then a decent idea of what's up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-09-2017, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:59:47-08:00","id":1046239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046132#post1046132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for that you didn't need to go to the book, I said &quot;hiding&quot; myself... But that reading to me is rules-lawery. I don't think that's the intended interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're talking about. The book doesn't give any alternative, Veiling is explicitly about concealment. To interpret it any other way is house ruling and means that you are shifting the conversation from a common ground founded in the book that we can all share to a made up lala land in your head. It's not polite to do that without warning. Hey, since you did though I'll jump right in. I took the liberty of looking up Veil in the dictionary to get some ideas on how we can expand the function of the Practice the way you want. Unfortunately, all the definitions are either about concealment (Just like the book, go figure!) or nuns and mushrooms. I guess we could make Veiling the nun and mushroom Practice? What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T20:56:32-08:00","id":1052371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044117-understanding-focused-mage-sight?p=1046239#post1046239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what you're talking about. The book doesn't give any alternative, Veiling is explicitly about concealment.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're super-focused on the wrong thing here and missing the whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage page 92</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concealment magic, of whatever type, can hide a target from Active Mage Sight, <b>but only if the concealment would logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So memory hole may be a veiling spell, but it's not going to be invisible to magesight. It will be visible as a Veiling spell, but if you were looking for the lost memories themselves, you would see neither memory nor the spell veiling the memory.<br /> <br /> Could you tell that there was something going on with passive sight? Maybe. I think that's definitely up to the table, storyteller and chronicle in question (for some of my games, the active continuous purging of memories would ping. For others, only the casting). But if a spell isn't actually <i>hiding</i> something, it doesn't itself also need to hide. The camo cover hides both the sniper and itself. The thirty foot wall only hides what's behind the thirty foot wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","name":"SiuiS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:39:29-08:00","id":1052454,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3652\" data-vbnamecard=\"3652\">SiuiS</a> I never said the spell was undetectable, I said it doesn't trigger PMS because Veiling spells don't because they are a concealment power. It'd be great if when you jumped into a conversation you actually understood the differing positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}